From 7247b755c3dbcf7829aa5da548b14bd276407a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Apr 2026 13:06:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [AI] feat: add Monthly Spending Target and Save by Date goal
 types with progress bar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Surfaces two previously unused template types (GoalTemplate, ByTemplate)
through a user-friendly UI, and adds a visual progress bar in the
automations modal for monthly spending targets.

Changes:
- Add 'monthly-target' (GoalTemplate) and 'by-date' (ByTemplate) to the
  displayTemplateTypes in constants.ts with plain-English labels
- Update reducer to handle 'goal' and 'by' template types instead of
  throwing, and add changeType cases for the two new display types
- Create MonthlyTargetAutomation/ReadOnly editor components (simple amount
  input; read-only shows "Monthly spending target: $X")
- Create ByDateAutomation/ReadOnly editor components (amount + month picker;
  read-only shows "Save $X by [month] ($Y/mo)")
- Create GoalProgressBar component that reads catBudgeted/catGoal from the
  envelope spreadsheet and renders a colour-coded bar (green ≥ 100%,
  yellow ≥ 50%, red < 50%)
- Integrate GoalProgressBar into BudgetAutomationsModal, shown when a
  monthly-target goal exists for the category
- Wrap the category-automations-edit modal in SheetNameProvider (current
  month) so spreadsheet bindings resolve correctly inside the modal
- Fix getDisplayTypeFromTemplate to correctly map 'goal' → 'monthly-target'
  and 'by' → 'by-date' instead of falling through to 'week'

